---
description: Testing and code quality rules for FinShield AI
alwaysApply: true
---

Testing philosophy:
- Write production-quality code with tests for critical behavior.
- Prefer deterministic unit tests for business logic: fraud detection pipeline, rules engine, risk scoring, feature engineering, case/alert workflow.
- Add integration tests for APIs, DB, Redis, and full transaction/alert flow.
- Mock external services: Event Hubs (or use test container), SendGrid, Twilio, Azure Blob/Key Vault (or local emulators); do not depend on live external APIs in normal test runs.

Testing expectations:
- Add tests for non-trivial service methods (fraud_detection_service, rules_engine_service, risk_scoring_service, case_service).
- Add tests for auth and RBAC (admin, analyst, investigator, viewer).
- Test rules engine conditions and actions; test ML pipeline with fixed fixtures or mocked model inference.
- Cover validation, failure, and edge cases (missing entity, rule timeout, model unavailable — graceful degradation to rules-only).
- Keep tests readable and isolated; use pytest + pytest-asyncio + httpx for backend; Vitest + RTL + Playwright for frontend per CLAUDE.md.

Code quality:
- Linting and formatting (ruff for Python; ESLint/Prettier for frontend); type hints / TypeScript types.
- Keep functions focused; refactor repeated logic into shared utilities when justified.

Do not:
- Add major logic without at least basic tests.
- Create brittle tests tied to unstable implementation details.
- Depend on live Azure, Twilio, or email in normal test runs.
